## 🎯 How Router-Outlet Works

The `<router-outlet>` in your [home.html](file:///c:/Users/HP/Desktop/Projects/chatApp/snChatFront/src/app/features/home/home.html#L22) acts as a placeholder where child route components will be rendered:

```
URL: /features/home/chat-list
├── Home Component (home.html)
│   ├── Navigation (always visible)
│   └── <router-outlet>
│       └── ChatList Component (rendered here)

URL: /features/home/settings
├── Home Component (home.html)
│   ├── Navigation (always visible)
│   └── <router-outlet>
│       └── Settings Component (rendered here)
```

When you click a navigation link with `routerLink="chat-list"`, Angular:
1. Updates the URL to `/features/home/chat-list`
2. Finds the matching child route
3. Renders the `ChatList` component inside the `<router-outlet>`
4. The navigation stays visible (it's part of the parent Home component)
